{
  "slug": "learn",
  "name": "Learn",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Research any topic online and create comprehensive learning guides with RAG-optimized indexes for your AI agents. `/learn react hooks` searches the web for ~20 sources, scores each on a 100-point scale across authority (3x), recency (2x), depth (2x), examples (2x), and uniqueness (1x), fetches only high-scoring sources, and writes a synthesized guide to `agent-knowledge/<topic>.md` with companion `resources/<topic>-sources.json` containing full source metadata. Six-stage methodology: progressive discovery, quality scoring, just-in-time extraction, synthesis, source citation, RAG optimization. Output shape designed for ingestion by Claude Code, OpenCode, and Codex agent-knowledge libraries.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **1 agent** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `learn` (Research any topic online and create learning guides)\n- **Agents** (1): `learn-agent` (Research topics online and create comprehensive learning guides with RAG indexes)\n- **Commands** (1): `learn` (Use when user asks to \"learn about topic\", \"research subject\", \"create learning guide\", \"build knowledge base\", \"study topic\",…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install learn@claude-community` from `agent-sh/learn`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
